Reports the Suunto D9 family's safety stop events, for libdivecomputer 0.9.0.

The D9 parser reads when a voluntary or mandatory safety stop begins and
ends, but upstream has reported them as no event since 2017, leaving only
the deco state on the samples. Shylog records the moment a stop becomes
mandatory (issue #80), so the image's dctool is built with this patch
(patch -p1) to report them.

--- a/src/suunto_d9_parser.c
+++ b/src/suunto_d9_parser.c
@@ -597,14 +597,14 @@
 					seconds = data[offset + 1];
 					switch (type & 0x7F) {
 					case 0x00: // Voluntary Safety Stop
-						sample.event.type = SAMPLE_EVENT_NONE;
+						sample.event.type = SAMPLE_EVENT_SAFETYSTOP_VOLUNTARY;
 						if (type & 0x80)
 							in_deco &= ~SAFETYSTOP;
 						else
 							in_deco |= SAFETYSTOP;
 						break;
 					case 0x01: // Mandatory Safety Stop - odd concept; model as deco stop
-						sample.event.type = SAMPLE_EVENT_NONE;
+						sample.event.type = SAMPLE_EVENT_SAFETYSTOP_MANDATORY;
 						if (type & 0x80)
 							in_deco &= ~DECOSTOP;
 						else
@@ -675,7 +675,7 @@
 							in_deco |= DEEPSTOP;
 						break;
 					case 0x14: // Mandatory Safety Stop - again, model as deco stop
-						sample.event.type = SAMPLE_EVENT_NONE;
+						sample.event.type = SAMPLE_EVENT_SAFETYSTOP_MANDATORY;
 						if (type & 0x80)
 							in_deco &= ~DECOSTOP;
 						else
